id, g dash-dot, b dashed. r stays below g and b on the shoulder; g and b are about 0.1 apart above D 3.0 and fall together by log H -1.8 (D 2.9). From log H -1.7 to -1.3 the three lines are one ink band about 0.1 thick (r lowest edge, g and b upper edge): r, g and b were traced through the same band centre there (differences below about 0.05 are not readable), and below log H -1.2 they coincide. Curves end at log H 1.0 (frame edge), D plateau about 0.12.","sensitivity: y is relative log sensitivity as printed (sensitivity = reciprocal of the exposure in J/cm2 giving minimum density + 1.0). Curves are drawn from about -0.7 up to the peak and down again: b 395-522 nm, g 482-603 nm, r 550-680 nm; each ends in a near-vertical drop, so the last few nm are only approximated on the 5 nm grid.","dyes: spectral diffuse density of the separated dyes (maximum 1.0 each) as printed; curves start at about 394 nm (yellow 396) and cyan ends at 711 nm (D 0.29). Yellow is not traced beyond 555 nm and magenta beyond 660 nm where they join the base line (about 0.01). Cyan and magenta cross near 437 nm (both about 0.035): the upper-left curve at 394 nm is cyan, the lower one magenta; yellow/magenta cross near 496 nm, yellow/cyan near 525 nm, magenta/cyan near 590 nm (D 0.43)."],"dyes":{"y":[[395.0,0.6046],[400.0,0.632],[405.0,0.6805],[410.0,0.7301],[415.0,0.7812],[420.0,0.8308],[425.0,0.8782],[430.0,0.921],[435.0,0.9573],[440.0,0.984],[445.0,0.9938],[450.0,0.9873],[455.0,0.9565],[460.0,0.9068],[465.0,0.8417],[470.0,0.7614],[475.0,0.6697],[480.0,0.5699],[485.0,0.4688],[490.0,0.3767],[495.0,0.3053],[500.0,0.24],[505.0,0.1834],[510.0,0.1396],[515.0,0.107],[520.0,0.0814],[525.0,0.0588],[530.0,0.0454],[535.0,0.0326],[540.0,0.0232],[545.0,0.0165],[550.0,0.0135],[555.0,0.0127]],"m":[[390.0,0.0392],[395.0,0.0392],[400.0,0.0348],[405.0,0.0308],[410.0,0.0271],[415.0,0.0256],[420.0,0.0241],[425.0,0.0241],[430.0,0.0256],[435.0,0.0343],[440.0,0.0346],[445.0,0.0417],[450.0,0.0511],[455.0,0.0614],[460